---
# This front matter (the YAML between the --- lines) is how Eleventy
# configures THIS specific template. "pagination" is the trick that
# turns one template file into two output files:
#   - "data" points at the list we built in src/_data/pages/home.js
#     (Eleventy sees this file's path and exposes it as pages.home.locales)
#   - "size: 1" means "give me one list item per generated page"
#   - "alias: locale" means "call that one item `locale` inside this template"
# So Eleventy runs this template TWICE — once with locale set to the
# Arabic entry, once with the English entry — and "permalink" (which
# reads locale.permalink) decides each time where the output HTML goes:
# /index.html for Arabic, /index-en.html for English.
pagination:
  data: pages.home.locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale.permalink }}"
---
{#
  TAQATHON - HOME PAGE TEMPLATE (src/pages/home.njk)
  ---------------------------------------------------
  This one file replaces what used to be two separate hand-written
  files: index.html (Arabic) and index-en.html (English). See the
  pagination front matter above for how "one template → two pages"
  actually works.

  Sections on this page (same content as the original site, just now
  pulled from data instead of typed directly into the HTML):
    - Hero: headline + 3 call-to-action buttons + hero photo
    - Countdown: live timer to a deadline (data-deadline attribute)
    - Announcements: list fetched client-side from a JSON file
    - About: "what you'll do" copy + prize amounts
    - CTA band: closing "get started" banner

  TO CUSTOMIZE:
    - Text (headings, button labels, prize amounts, etc.) → edit
      src/_data/copy/home.ar.json and home.en.json, NOT this file.
    - Shared nav/footer text → src/_data/site.ar.json / site.en.json.
    - Countdown deadline → the "deadline" field inside the two
      home.*.json files above (ISO 8601 format, e.g. "2026-09-01T00:00:00+03:00").
    - Page structure/layout (adding a new section, changing markup) →
      this file, inside the {% block content %} below.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% block pageHead %}
{#
  Visual system v2 (Phase 3): these three fonts are only used by the
  editorial hero/About redesign below — no other page loads them yet,
  hence a page-scoped pageHead block instead of adding them to the
  global Cairo/Poppins link in base.njk. Big Shoulders Display for the
  oversized Latin headline, Tajawal for the Arabic equivalent (this
  design's own choice — distinct from the site-wide Cairo used
  everywhere else, scoped to just .dz-display/.dz-about-heading via
  the [dir="rtl"] overrides below), DM Mono for the small tracked
  metadata labels.
#}
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Big+Shoulders+Display:wght@600;700;800&family=Tajawal:wght@700;800;900&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
{% endblock %}
{% block pageStyle %}
{#
  Editorial redesign, through several direct-feedback rounds (Phase 3,
  visual system v2). Current state (round 7):

  Three background tones total, each used with intent:
    --color-cream — Hero and About. The two most "editorial" sections.
    --color-sky — Countdown AND the CTA band, as of round 7 ("make the
      CTA band the same blue as Countdown"): grouping the page's two
      "do something" moments (check the deadline / take the final
      action) under one tone, by purpose rather than by position.
    --color-stone — navbar + footer, chrome's own tone, used nowhere
      else on the page (round 7: "a different color that is not used
      in the page but does not clash," after --color-pearl then reused
      --color-sky both turned out too close to something else on the
      page once the content-section palette itself changed under them).

  With background no longer doing all the work of telling sections
  apart, each one gets ONE small, restrained signal instead — shape,
  icon, or texture, never a color shift: the Hero/CTA's soft blurred
  orbs, the Countdown's flowing wave, the Announcements' faint dotted
  grid, and About's own two-column photo+text layout plus its stat
  cards. About specifically carries NO decorative texture layer (round
  3 had a node-network SVG there; direct feedback called that section
  "too many colors" and it was cut, not brought back since).

  Dark navy is a small ACCENT only, never a section background: the
  hero's stat bar, About's two stat cards, nothing more. Accent-color
  rule unchanged: amber only reads as text on those small dark
  accents; terra reads as text on the light tones. Buttons stay self-
  contained (amber bg + navy text) regardless of section.

  Round 8: dark mode built as the mirror the earlier rounds planned
  for — navy (well, --bg/--surface, see common.css) as the base
  everywhere, cream/sky demoted to accents. See the big "DARK MODE
  MIRROR" comment block further down for the full account of what
  flips and why; the short version is nothing here in light mode
  needed to change, dark mode is entirely additive [data-bs-theme="dark"]
  overrides layered on top.
#}
.dz-hero{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); overflow:hidden; position:relative; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
{# Same faint navy hairline as the navbar/footer border (common.css)
   — trying it at every real color change between sections (cream ->
   sky -> cream -> sky) so each band reads as a deliberate, separated
   region rather than blurring into its neighbor. Skipped between
   Announcements and About below since both are cream with no color
   change between them — that boundary is intentionally seamless per
   the earlier "keep everything below the hero the same color" call. #}
{#
  Every section's decorative layer sits at z-index:0 with
  pointer-events:none (so it's inert — never intercepts clicks or gets
  picked up by a screen reader), and every section's actual content
  wrapper gets position:relative + z-index:1 to sit above it. Same
  pattern repeated per section below rather than one generic rule, so
  each section's specific content wrapper (.dz-hero-grid, .container,
  etc.) can be targeted precisely.
#}
.dz-hero::before{
  content:""; position:absolute; top:-15%; inset-inline-end:-8%; width:460px; height:460px;
  background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(196,64,26,.08), transparent 70%);
  border-radius:50%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
}
.dz-hero-grid{ position:relative; z-index:1; display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); align-items:stretch; min-height:560px; }
@media (max-width:991.98px){ .dz-hero-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; min-height:auto; } }
.dz-hero-copy{ display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; padding:3rem clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 5rem); }
.dz-display{
  font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700;
  font-size:clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 5.5rem); line-height:.95; letter-spacing:-.01em;
  margin:0 0 1rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .dz-display{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0; }
.dz-subtitle{ font-size:1.15rem; color:var(--color-dust); margin-bottom:1rem; max-width:32rem; }
.dz-body{ color:var(--color-dust); max-width:32rem; margin-bottom:1.75rem; }
.dz-hero-photo{ position:relative; min-height:320px; }
.dz-hero-photo img{
  width:100%; height:100%; min-height:320px; object-fit:cover; display:block;
  clip-path:polygon(12% 0, 100% 0, 100% 100%, 0% 100%);
}
[dir="rtl"] .dz-hero-photo img{ clip-path:polygon(0 0, 88% 0, 100% 100%, 0 100%); }
@media (max-width:991.98px){ .dz-hero-photo img{ clip-path:none; min-height:280px; } }
{#
  The stat bar is the hero's one small dark accent — exactly the kind
  of use the round-3 rule allows (a stat bar, a badge — never a full
  section). It's also a quiet preview of where the dark/light balance
  flips once dark mode exists.
#}
.dz-stat-bar{
  position:absolute; bottom:1.5rem; inset-inline-end:1.5rem;
  background:var(--brand-dark); color:var(--color-cream);
  border-radius:.5rem; padding:1rem 1.25rem; font-size:.85rem;
  box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
  display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.5rem; min-width:220px;
}
.dz-stat-bar .dz-stat-row{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; }
.dz-stat-bar .dz-stat-label{
  font-family:var(--font-mono-label); color:var(--color-mist); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; font-size:.7rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .dz-stat-bar .dz-stat-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
.dz-stat-bar .dz-stat-value{ font-weight:600; }
@media (max-width:575.98px){ .dz-stat-bar{ position:static; margin-top:1rem; inset-inline-end:auto; } }

/* ===== Countdown: --color-sky, pale baby blue, + a flowing wave layer ===== */
.gb-band{ background:var(--color-sky); color:var(--brand-dark); position:relative; overflow:hidden; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
.gb-band .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; }
.dz-deco-wave{ position:absolute; inset:0; width:100%; height:100%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0; }
{# stroke set via CSS (not the SVG's stroke="" attribute) specifically
   so dark mode can override it below — a CSS property always beats an
   SVG presentation attribute, so this is the one styling hook this
   inline SVG actually has. #}
.dz-wave-line-a{ stroke:#00284C; }
.dz-wave-line-b{ stroke:#E8952B; }
.count-box{
position:relative; background:rgba(232,149,43,.07); border:1px solid rgba(232,149,43,.25);
border-radius:1rem; max-width:650px; margin-inline:auto; padding:2rem;
}
.count-tile{
background:#fff; border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.1);
color:var(--brand-dark); border-radius:.75rem; width:56px; height:56px;
display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:700;
}
.count-label{ font-size:.8rem; color:var(--color-dust); }

{#
  Round 5: cream now, not its own linen tone — direct instruction was
  everything from Announcements down through the CTA band matches
  Hero's cream exactly (Countdown explicitly excluded, stays sky), and
  sections tell themselves apart with shape/icon/texture instead of a
  shifting background. Announcements already had exactly that in the
  dotted-grid layer below; it just needed the color underneath it to
  change, not the idea.
#}
/* ===== Announcements: --color-cream (matches Hero), + a faint dotted grid ===== */
#announcements{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); position:relative; overflow:hidden; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
#announcements::before{
  content:""; position:absolute; inset:0; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
  background-image:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(0,40,76,.07) 1px, transparent 1px);
  background-size:24px 24px;
}
#announcements .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; }
.dz-muted-on-cream{ color:var(--color-dust); }
.dz-muted-on-navy{ color:var(--color-mist); }
.ann-list{ max-width:900px; margin:0 auto; display:grid; gap:12px; }
{#
  The original Arabic and English pages mirrored this card's padding
  and icon position (icon on the right for RTL, left for LTR) by
  writing out two separate, near-identical <style> blocks. Here it's
  one rule with an {% if %} branch instead — same visual result, half
  the CSS to maintain.
#}
.ann-card{
position:relative; background:#fff; border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08);
border-radius:12px; {% if locale.dir == "rtl" %}padding:16px 56px 16px 16px;{% else %}padding:16px 16px 16px 56px;{% endif %}
box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.04);
}
.ann-icon{
position:absolute; {% if locale.dir == "rtl" %}right:16px;{% else %}left:16px;{% endif %} top:16px; width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:8px;
display:grid; place-items:center; font-size:16px;
}
.ann-date{ font-size:.8rem; color:var(--color-dust); }
.ann-text{ color:var(--brand-dark); }
{#
  terra for the urgent type (deadline) — passes on every light tone
  (4.5+:1, see common.css). amber does NOT pass on any of them (per
  the accent-color rule) so it's not used here at all; the other types
  use --brand-dark instead, still a real distinction from terra, just
  not a third hue.
#}
.type-deadline .ann-icon{ background:rgba(196,64,26,.12); color:var(--color-terra); }
.type-update .ann-icon, .type-schedule .ann-icon{ background:rgba(0,40,76,.08); color:var(--brand-dark); }
.type-general .ann-icon{ background:rgba(0,40,76,.06); color:var(--color-dust); }

{#
  Round 4: dropped the marquee entirely (direct feedback — "the moving
  bar"). It was originally justified as marking the one hard color
  transition between a light Act 1 and a dark Act 2; round 3 already
  made the whole page light, so that transition it was marking no
  longer exists — removing it isn't just accommodating a preference,
  it's also the more honest choice now that there's nothing left for
  it to divide. Announcements now runs straight into About with just
  the background tint doing the work, same as every other section
  transition on the page.
#}

{#
  Round 4: About simplified — direct feedback that the heading and
  everything under it had too many colors going at once (sage bg +
  terra heading + navy body + terra icons + amber/navy stat cells +
  a node-network texture layer, all in one section). Dropped terra
  from this section entirely and the decorative texture layer with
  it — heading/icons/body are all navy now, monochrome against the
  sage tint, the same restraint Hero already had (one accent color —
  terra there, none here — plus navy, nothing more). The stat cells
  stay as About's one deliberate accent moment (navy+amber), not
  removed, since two small cards were never the "too much" part.

  Round 5: sage retired too — same instruction as Announcements above,
  cream now instead of its own tone. What still tells About apart from
  Hero/Announcements/CTA at a glance is its own content shape (a photo
  + text two-column layout none of the others use) and the navy/amber
  stat cells, not a background color anymore.
#}
.dz-about{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
.dz-about-heading{
  font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; color:var(--brand-dark);
  font-size:clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem); line-height:1.05; letter-spacing:-.01em; margin-bottom:1rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .dz-about-heading{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0; }
.dz-about-body{ color:var(--color-dust); max-width:38rem; margin-bottom:1.75rem; }
.dz-about-list{ color:var(--brand-dark); list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0 0 2rem; }
.dz-about-list li{ display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:.6rem; margin-bottom:.6rem; }
.dz-about-list .bi{ color:var(--brand-dark); margin-top:.2rem; }
{#
  The stat cells are About's small dark accent (same allowance as the
  hero's stat bar) — the one deliberately navy element inside an
  otherwise light section, there specifically to make these two
  numbers punch through.
#}
.dz-stats-grid{
  display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px,1fr)); gap:1px;
  background:rgba(0,40,76,.1); border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.1);
  border-radius:.75rem; overflow:hidden;
}
.dz-stat-cell{ background:var(--brand-dark); padding:1.5rem 1.25rem; }
.dz-stat-num{ font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; color:var(--color-amber); font-size:1.85rem; line-height:1.1; margin-bottom:.4rem; display:block; }
[dir="rtl"] .dz-stat-num{ font-family:inherit; font-weight:800; }
.dz-stat-cell-label{ font-family:var(--font-mono-label); font-size:.7rem; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--color-mist); }
[dir="rtl"] .dz-stat-cell-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }

{#
  Round 5: slate retired, cream. Round 7: cream retired too — direct
  instruction to make the CTA band ("ابقَ على المسار") the same blue
  as Countdown. The two now share --color-sky: both are "do something"
  moments (check the deadline / take the final action), so tying them
  to the same tone groups them by PURPOSE, not just position on the
  page. The blurred amber orb still marks this as its own moment
  within that shared tone.
#}
/* ===== CTA band: --color-sky (matches Countdown), + a blurred orb ===== */
.cta-band{ background:var(--color-sky); color:var(--color-dust); position:relative; overflow:hidden; }
.cta-band::before{
  content:""; position:absolute; bottom:-25%; inset-inline-start:-8%; width:400px; height:400px;
  background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(232,149,43,.14), transparent 70%);
  border-radius:50%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
}
.cta-band .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; }
.cta-band h3{ color:var(--color-terra); }
.cta-band .btn{ background:var(--color-amber); border:0; color:var(--brand-dark); font-weight:700; }
.cta-band .btn:hover{ filter:brightness(1.05); color:var(--brand-dark); }

{#
  ===== DARK MODE MIRROR (Phase 3, round 8) =====

  Everything above this point is untouched — dark mode is purely
  additive [data-bs-theme="dark"] overrides layered on top, same
  approach common.css already uses for the navbar/footer.

  THE MIRROR, AS PLANNED BACK IN ROUND 3: light mode is three light
  tones (cream/sky/stone) with navy as a small accent (the hero stat
  bar, About's two stat cells). Dark mode flips that: --color-cream
  and --color-sky are redefined in common.css's [data-bs-theme="dark"]
  block to reuse the site's existing dark tokens (--bg/--surface) —
  so every section background here flips FOR FREE, nothing to change
  in this file for that part. What this file still has to handle by
  hand is everything that isn't a plain background:var(--color-*):
  text colors hardcoded to var(--brand-dark)/var(--color-dust) (those
  don't flip on their own — --brand-dark is the site's fixed identity
  color, deliberately the same in both modes), and the accent-color
  swap below.

  ACCENT SWAP: light mode's rule is "amber only reads on the dark
  neutral, terra only reads on the light neutral" (verified by
  contrast math in common.css). Once the main section backgrounds ARE
  the dark neutral, amber becomes the section's primary accent
  (badge, CTA heading, decorative orbs) — taking over terra's role.
  Terra doesn't disappear: it moves to the hero stat bar and About's
  stat cells, which flip from "small dark accent on a light section"
  to "small LIGHT accent on a dark section" (background flips to a
  fixed, theme-invariant cream — not var(--color-cream), which is
  dark in this mode — same self-contained-regardless-of-theme idea
  already used by count-tile and every button), and terra is what
  passes contrast on THAT light surface (4.83:1, verified) the way
  amber no longer does (2.26:1, fails) once the surface underneath it
  is light again.
#}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-hero,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .gb-band,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] #announcements,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-about{
  color:var(--text);
  border-bottom-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08);
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-hero::before{
  background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(232,149,43,.10), transparent 70%);
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-subtitle,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-body,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-about-body,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .count-label,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-muted-on-cream{ color:var(--muted); }
{#
  Stat bar/cells: the one deliberate structural flip, not just a
  color swap — background goes from --brand-dark to a fixed cream
  hex (never var(--color-cream), which now points at the dark
  background these elements are meant to stand OUT from), text goes
  from cream to navy, and the accent number swaps amber → terra to
  match (see the swap explanation above).
#}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-stat-bar{
  background:#FAF8F4; color:var(--brand-dark);
  box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.45);
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-stat-bar .dz-stat-label{ color:var(--color-dust); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-stat-cell{ background:#FAF8F4; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-stat-num{ color:var(--color-terra); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-stat-cell-label{ color:var(--color-dust); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-wave-line-a{ stroke:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-wave-line-b{ stroke:var(--color-amber); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .count-box{ background:rgba(232,149,43,.09); border-color:rgba(232,149,43,.3); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] #announcements::before{
  background-image:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,.06) 1px, transparent 1px);
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ann-card{
  background:var(--surface); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08);
  box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ann-date{ color:var(--muted); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ann-text{ color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .type-deadline .ann-icon{ background:rgba(232,149,43,.14); color:var(--color-amber); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .type-update .ann-icon,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .type-schedule .ann-icon{ background:rgba(255,255,255,.08); color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .type-general .ann-icon{ background:rgba(255,255,255,.06); color:var(--muted); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-about-heading{ color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-about-list,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .dz-about-list .bi{ color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .cta-band{ color:var(--muted); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .cta-band h3{ color:var(--color-amber); }

/* ===== Reveal ===== */
.reveal{ opacity:0; transform:translateY(12px); transition:opacity .6s ease, transform .6s ease; }
.reveal.in{ opacity:1; transform:none; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
.reveal{ transition:none !important; opacity:1 !important; transform:none !important; }
}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
{#
  Editorial hero (Phase 3, visual system v2): every string here is an
  existing home.*.json field, just re-laid-out — hero.title/subtitle/
  body/ctas/badge are unchanged from the previous design, nothing
  invented. The two new lines in the floating stat bar (deadline +
  status) are built from the same countdown.deadline value the
  countdown section below already uses, not new facts — "Open"/
  "Closed" is computed client-side in pageScript by comparing that
  deadline to the current date, same idea as the countdown timer
  itself, so it flips on its own after the deadline passes instead of
  needing a manual edit.
#}
<section class="dz-hero">
<div class="dz-hero-grid">
  <div class="dz-hero-copy reveal">
    <h1 class="dz-display">{{ locale.content.hero.title }}</h1>
    <p class="dz-subtitle">{{ locale.content.hero.subtitle }}</p>
    <p class="dz-body">{{ locale.content.hero.body }}</p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {% for cta in locale.content.hero.ctas %}
      <a class="btn {{ cta.btnClass }}" href="{{ cta.href }}">
        <i class="bi {{ cta.icon }} {{ locale.content.hero.iconMarginClass }}"></i> {{ cta.label }}
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="dz-hero-photo reveal">
    <img src="{{ locale.content.hero.image.src }}"
         alt="{{ locale.content.hero.image.alt }}"
         loading="eager" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000">
    <div class="dz-stat-bar">
      <div class="dz-stat-row">
        <span class="dz-stat-label">{{ locale.content.hero.metaDeadlineLabel }}</span>
        <span class="dz-stat-value" id="heroDeadlineValue"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="dz-stat-row">
        <span class="dz-stat-label">{{ locale.content.hero.metaStatusLabel }}</span>
        <span class="dz-stat-value" id="heroStatusValue">{{ locale.content.hero.metaStatusOpen }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- COUNTDOWN -->
<section class="gb-band py-5">
{#
  Decorative wave layer (Phase 3, round 3): purely atmospheric, no
  information of its own — aria-hidden, and it sits behind the actual
  content via z-index (see .dz-deco-wave/.gb-band .container in
  pageStyle). Two soft flowing lines, navy and amber, at very low
  opacity so they read as texture, not as competing content.
#}
<svg class="dz-deco-wave" viewBox="0 0 800 200" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
  <path class="dz-wave-line-a" d="M0,110 C150,190 350,30 500,110 C650,190 750,70 800,110" fill="none" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.05"/>
  <path class="dz-wave-line-b" d="M0,150 C150,70 350,190 500,150 C650,110 750,170 800,130" fill="none" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.08"/>
</svg>
<div class="container text-center">
  <div class="count-box p-4 reveal">
    <div class="mb-2 fw-semibold">{{ locale.content.countdown.label }}</div>
    {#
      data-deadline is read by the countdown script down in pageScript.
      This is still the ORIGINAL (already-past) deadline from the live
      site — Phase 0's job was to prove the template pipeline works,
      not to change content. Fixing this date is Phase 1, item 1.
    #}
    <div id="deadline" class="d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center gap-3"
         data-deadline="{{ locale.content.countdown.deadline }}">
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="count-tile"><span id="ddays">00</span></div>
        <div class="count-label">{{ locale.content.countdown.units.days }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="count-tile"><span id="dhours">00</span></div>
        <div class="count-label">{{ locale.content.countdown.units.hours }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="count-tile"><span id="dmins">00</span></div>
        <div class="count-label">{{ locale.content.countdown.units.mins }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="count-tile"><span id="dsecs">00</span></div>
        <div class="count-label">{{ locale.content.countdown.units.secs }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ANNOUNCEMENTS -->
{# The actual announcement cards are NOT rendered here by Nunjucks at
   build time — this section starts empty on purpose. A script down in
   pageScript fetches announcements-ar.json / announcements.json in the
   visitor's browser and fills in #ann-wrap with JS, exactly like the
   original site did. That's why there's no {% for %} loop in this
   section the way there is in Hero/About below. #}
<section class="py-5" id="announcements">
<div class="container">
  <div class="text-center dz-muted-on-cream mb-3">{{ locale.content.announcements.heading }}</div>
  <div id="ann-wrap" class="ann-list"><!-- injected by JS --></div>
</div>
</section>

{#
  About (Phase 3, visual system v2): heading/body/list items are all
  unchanged existing fields. The old inline "trophy icon + prize
  amounts" line is now its own stat cell below instead of a bullet in
  the list — same prize.amounts data, just presented as a number
  instead of a sentence fragment, so it isn't shown twice. Track count
  (3) is real and already reflected on the Registration page (three
  track cards, names still placeholder) — see tracksStatValue in
  home.*.json. Deliberately only 2 stat cells, not the 4 the reference
  mockup used: duration/participant-count/university-count aren't in
  any data file, and this project's rule is flag what's missing rather
  than invent it. No decorative texture layer here (round 3 had a
  node-network SVG; removed in round 4 along with the extra accent
  color — see the big comment above .dz-about in pageStyle).
#}
<section class="dz-about py-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row g-4 align-items-center">
    <div class="col-lg-5 reveal">
      <img class="w-100 rounded-2xl shadow-soft"
           src="{{ locale.content.about.image.src }}"
           alt="{{ locale.content.about.image.alt }}"
           loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1400" height="500">
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-7 reveal">
      <h2 class="dz-about-heading">{{ locale.content.about.heading }}</h2>
      <p class="dz-about-body">{{ locale.content.about.body }}</p>
      <ul class="dz-about-list">
        {% for item in locale.content.about.listCol1 %}
        <li><i class="bi {{ item.icon }}"></i> {{ item.text }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
        <li><i class="bi {{ locale.content.about.listCol2Extra.icon }}"></i> {{ locale.content.about.listCol2Extra.text }}</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="dz-stats-grid">
        <div class="dz-stat-cell">
          <span class="dz-stat-num">
            {% for amount in locale.content.about.prize.amounts %}{{ amount }}{% if not loop.last %} / {% endif %}{% endfor %}
          </span>
          <span class="dz-stat-cell-label">{{ locale.content.about.prizeStatLabel }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="dz-stat-cell">
          <span class="dz-stat-num">{{ locale.content.about.tracksStatValue }}</span>
          <span class="dz-stat-cell-label">{{ locale.content.about.tracksStatLabel }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- CTA BAND -->
<section class="cta-band py-5 text-center">
<div class="container reveal">
  <h3 class="fw-bold mb-2" style="font-size:1.7rem;">{{ locale.content.cta.heading }}</h3>
  <p class="mb-4" style="font-size:1.05rem;">
    {{ locale.content.cta.body }}
  </p>
  <a class="btn {{ locale.content.cta.buttonExtraClass }}px-4 py-2" href="{{ locale.content.cta.buttonHref }}">
    {{ locale.content.cta.buttonLabel }}
